{"version":1,"kind":"summary","errors":45,"warnings":0,"explanations":{"E0033":"# E0033: name that is not in scope\n\nA name in an expression must be a binding in scope: a `let`, a parameter, or a binding made by `for`, `if let` or `while let`. A binding is in scope from its declaration to the end of its block.\n\nThe name of a type is no binding: `f64` or a class's name read as a value is [E0105](E0105.md). So is the name of a function read as a value.\n\nWhen a binding in scope has a similar name, the error offers it as an unsafe fix. The unsafe fix may be wrong: the name could be a binding that was never declared.\n\n## Why\n\nSisu does not resolve a misspelled name on its own. A misspelled name, or one used after its block has ended, would otherwise read some other value or none.\n\n## Broken\n\n```sisu\nfn main() {\n    let total = 3\n    print(totl)\n}\n```\n\n## Fixed\n\n```sisu\nfn main() {\n    let total = 3\n    print(total)\n}\n```\n","E0063":"# E0063: field or method that does not exist\n\nA field read or a method call must name a member of the receiver's type: a field or method of its class, the array methods `len()`, `sum()` and `contains(x)`, the `string` methods `len()`, `chars()`, `bytes()` and `words()`, or the methods of `f64` and `i64`, such as `x.sqrt()` and `n.max(m)`. A built-in type's name takes a constant: `f64.pi`, `f64.tau`, `f64.e`, `f64.infinity`, `f64.nan`, `f64.max`, `f64.min_positive` and `f64.epsilon`. No other type has any, so `i64.max` is this error too. A method of `f64` is no method of `i64`: `n.sqrt()` with an `i64` `n` is this error too. A constructor's labels must name fields of its class, or of the labeled payload of its variant. The methods of an enum count as methods of its type, but its value has no fields: that is [E0121](E0121.md).\n\nWhen a member of the receiver's type has a similar name, the error offers it as an unsafe fix. The unsafe fix may be wrong: the name could be a member that was never written. For `let x = 2.5` and `x.sqrtt()`, the unsafe fix is `sqrt`; for `f64.PI`, it is `pi`.\n\nThe same error is reported for a method call on a value of a type parameter: the type parameter has only the methods of its bounds. When exactly one interface of the program declares a method of that name, and it takes no type parameters, the help adds the bound: for `x.area()` on a value of type `T`, `add a bound: T: Shape`. If `T` has bounds already, the help lists them with the new one.\n\n## Why\n\nSisu does not resolve a misspelled member name on its own. A misspelled name would otherwise read some other value or run some other code.\n\n## Broken\n\n```sisu\nclass Point {\n    x: i64\n}\n\nfn main() {\n    let p = Point(x: 1)\n    print(p.y)\n}\n```\n\n## Fixed\n\n```sisu\nclass Point {\n    x: i64\n}\n\nfn main() {\n    let p = Point(x: 1)\n    print(p.x)\n}\n```\n"}}
